cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PluggyBot: a simulated, hardware-honest robot and the autonomous agent that lives in it"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Holland
    given-names: Ben
repository-code: "https://github.com/benholland1024/pluggybot"
url: "https://rooftop-media.org/experiments/pluggyworld"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  PluggyBot is the simulation behind PluggyWorld. Two humanoid robots live
  in a small simulated neighborhood, and a language model makes their
  decisions. Each robot is built in MuJoCo from real parts that can be
  bought, with their datasheets' limits and noise. The robots charge
  themselves, take jobs for points, write small programs to do those jobs,
  and can die. The project measures how far such an agent gets on its own, and
  where it stops.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - humanoid
  - MuJoCo
  - LLM agents
  - embodied AI
  - benchmark
